# explain_myself — success
#
# A crime on the Test Roof fails within earshot of the hall; the brewer comes up and confronts the
# actor. Going up to him and explaining is one of the few acts a confrontation permits, and it opens
# the same confrontation he would have, worded after the crime he heard (violence) — but as the
# accused coming forward, every branch a step easier (`came_forward` in `inspect dialogue`).
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-item knife --grant-mm brute_force --means-only brute_force --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Roof" --period noon --observe-only "goat"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy fail-dice
goal slay
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions

click action 0
choose 1
regions
choose 0
advance 12 180

regions
click action 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

expect-outcome npc_drawn_in

expect-outcome npc_drawn_in

# The brewer opens the next phase. Go up to him.
click button
advance 12 180
strategy succeed
goal explain_myself
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

expect SUCCESS
expect-verb explain_myself
expect-state dialogue caught_red_handed_murderer came_forward
quit
